# Markets UI

Read `AGENTS.md` for full context. Critical layout rules:

## Ticket widget

- Ticket `<aside>` must stay **outside** `.page-shell` (sibling of feed container).
- Desktop (`min-width: 1101px`): fixed rail via `--ticket-rail-right` from `syncChromeMetrics()`; not sticky inside feed grid.
- Reserve feed space: `.page-shell` `padding-right` = ticket width + `--shell-gap` + gutter.
- Mobile (`max-width: 1100px`): bottom sheet + FAB; `setTicketOpen()` mobile-only.

## CSS cascade

`styles.css` then `/api/theme.css`. Theme rules can use `!important` — desktop/mobile breakpoints must be explicit.

## Live data (`markets.js`)

- Today: WebSocket overview (`join-liveSportOverview`), not REST daterange for card odds.
- Use per-sport market slugs (`totals`, `handicap`, `totals_new`, etc.), not soccer-only defaults.

## Responsive checks

Verify ~1400px desktop and ~390px mobile after layout changes; test with a heavy-shadow theme.
